;; What this case exercises; edit by hand.  `bb corpus-accept' leaves it alone.
(:book "A new reference grammar of modern Spanish (2019)"
 :source "Espanol/A new reference grammar of modern Spanish (2019).pdf"
 :page 22
 :exercises "Future-work 11 evidence: parallel vertical flows.  The gender lists
set Spanish in a left lane and its gloss in a right lane; poppler
serves the lanes row-interleaved and the render braids them into
pseudo-prose (la nao ship (archaic) la Gestapo the Gestapo ...),
with leftover lane fragments as loose lines.  Reading a lane to its
end before the next is the FW11 fix; this golden records the braid
deliberately.  The page's real prose - the fruit and nut paragraphs
above the list - must keep flowing.  The dropped line is the
folio-merged running head.  The budget is the lane braid."
 :budget (:mid-sentence 2))
